## #01 — Read the entry first
ENTRY.md is the self-contained brief: role, question, targets, reading order, environment, permissions and stop points. 06 holds the supplied reasons. RETURN-TEMPLATE.md is the return shape.

## #02 — Method
Read the target section first, then the interface contract and the record groups. For each operation, say what input it needs, what it may decide by itself, and what it must leave to Prime or the Director. You may propose a different split or a different first slice if you can show why.

## #03 — Case C01
A return arrives with a Hostile finding that contradicts a Director decision. Walk it through intake, review and find. Where could it be lost or silently promoted?

## #04 — Case C02
Prime wants to reuse a prior experiment on the same subject page. Which operation must expose that, and from what record?

## #05 — Case C03
A package is prepared for a ZIP-only recipient, and one required source is an image that was never committed. Which operation should stop it, and with what message?

## #06 — Return
Return one file in the RETURN-TEMPLATE.md shape to the destination named in ENTRY.md. Keep Hostile, Factfind, Overflow and Unprompted even when empty.

